          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two different digits are selected without replacement from {1,2,3,4,5}. The first digit forms the tens digit and the second forms the units digit. Find the probability that the resulting two-digit number is greater than 40. Give your answer as a fraction in simplest form."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 4,
      "primary_outcome": "2.2",
      "secondary_outcomes": [],
      "response": {
